==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[whobub]] {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
Perhaps from Irish; compare Irish ''[[ababú]]!'' (a battle-cry), Gaelic ''[[ub|ub! ub!]]'' (expressing contempt, etc.), ''[[ubh ubh]]!'' (expressing disgust).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhʌbʌb/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ʌb|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[confuse]]d [[uproar]], [[commotion]], [[tumult]] or [[racket]].
#* John Milton, '' Paradise Lost''
#*: At length a universal '''hubbub''' wild
#*: Of stunning sounds and voices all confused,
#*: Borne through the hollow dark, assaults his ear
#*: With loudest vehemence.

====Synonyms====
* See also [[Wikisaurus:commotion]]

